  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focus-management-apis:locked-for-focus\n\n`locked for focus` is used to prevent calling focus() on the same element synchronously, this doesn't seem to be implemented in Webkit and Blink, and Gecko seems to have it half implemented. \n\nA testcase is https://codepen.io/sefeng/pen/mydQwjJ, clicking the \"click me\" input makes it to be focused in Webkit/Blink, and Gecko doesn't focus anything. If it's correctly implemented, `input2` should be focused I think. \n\nAnother test case is `data:text/html,<input onfocus=\"this.nextSibling.focus();\"><input onfocus=\"this.previousSibling.focus();\">`, Webkit/Blink seems to just rely on the `too much recursion` error. \n\n",
